You are given a special linked list of length n where each node contains an additional pointer called random. This random pointer can point to any node in the linked list or it can be null.

Your task is to create a deep copy (or clone) of this linked list.

A deep copy means:

You must create n brand-new nodes.

Each new node must have the exact same value as its corresponding original node.

The next pointers of the new nodes must link together in the exact same order as the original list.

The random pointers of the new nodes must point to the new nodes in your copied list, perfectly mirroring how the random pointers connected the nodes in the original list.

Crucial Rule: None of the pointers in your new list should point back to any nodes in the original list. You must return the head of this brand-new, completely independent copied list.

